# Unified bank-decline copy lock

## Canonical rule

**When the bank, card issuer or card network declines a payment, the customer sees the same popup for every payment method — Apple Pay, Google Pay, saved card, new card, 3DS card.** The wording never depends on the payment method and never blames ONECAB, Apple Pay, Google Pay or Revolut.

### Booking / new payment

- Title: `Payment declined by your bank`
- Message: `Your bank declined this payment. Please check your card, use another card, or choose another payment method.`
- Buttons: `Choose another card` / `Cancel`

### Trip modification

- Title: `Payment declined by your bank`
- Message: `Your bank declined the payment for this trip change. Please check your card or contact your bank, then try the change again.`
- Button: `OK` only

No card switch is offered mid-trip: a fare increase must increment the **same** Revolut order, and a second pre-authorisation/order is forbidden (see `revolut-incremental-auth-primary-lock.mdc`). Original destination/stops/fare stay unchanged.

## What counts as a bank decline

Use the unified copy **only** for a provider decline reason attributed to the issuer/card (any spelling/casing, Revolut or card-network equivalent):

- issuer_decline / issuer_declined / card_declined
- do_not_honour / do_not_honor
- insufficient_funds
- expired_card, lost_card, stolen_card, restricted_card, pick_up_card
- card_not_supported
- transaction_not_allowed_for_cardholder
- invalid_cvv, invalid_expiry, invalid_pin, pin_try_exceeded
- withdrawal_limit_exceeded, withdrawal_frequency_exceeded
- new_card_not_unblocked, invalid_account
- authentication_required after failed authorisation; 3DS / customer challenge **failed**

## Never bank-decline copy

These get neutral payment copy (no bank blame):

- high_risk, suspected_fraud (may be Revolut risk tools)
- issuer_not_available, technical_error, timeouts, unknown/missing reason
- invalid_merchant and other merchant configuration errors
- form/data errors (email, amount, address, country, cardholder name, phone)
- internal failures: `persist_failed`, `INCREMENT_CONFIRM_PERSIST_FAILED`, provider technical increment failure
- a bare `declined` / `failed` state with no issuer reason

3DS challenge **abandoned** / rejected by customer, and wallet sheet dismissal, are **cancellations** — not declines.

## Wallet wording

`Apple Pay …` / `Google Pay …` wording is allowed **only** when the wallet itself is cancelled, unavailable, not set up, or fails before card authorisation. After token handoff, resolve the provider decline reason (same order/session reconcile) before choosing copy — never default a post-handoff failure to wallet wording.

## Do not

- Show different decline wording per payment method
- Show "Apple Pay couldn't complete this payment" / "Google Pay couldn't complete this payment" / "ONECAB could not take payment" for a bank/card decline
- Keep a separate "Insufficient funds" title, or put a decline under "Booking didn't complete"
- Map technical, risk, internal or unknown failures to the bank-decline popup
- Keep separate decline lists in client and backend that disagree
- Pass raw provider/internal text to the customer
- Offer "Choose another card" for a trip-modification decline
- Change Revolut increment, capture, idempotency or create a second order to support decline copy

